  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Want to 'reset' ties with India, should be done through bilateral discussions: Bangladesh",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/bangladesh-wants-to-reset-ties-with-india/article71464479.ece",
      "description": "State Minister for Foreign Affairs Humaiun Kobir said Bangladesh needs to move beyond what he described as an “excessive preoccupation” with India and approach its relationship with New Delhi in a balanced manner",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-09-13T19:14:18"
    },
    {
      "title": "Want to 'reset' ties, build new bilateral engagement with India: Bangladesh",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/want-to-reset-ties-build-new-bilateral-engagement-with-india-bangladesh-126091300708_1.html",
      "description": "Bangladesh on Sunday said it wants to \"reset\" its relationship with India and build a new bilateral engagement based on mutual interests, while describing ties during the tenure of deposed prime minister Sheikh Hasina as \"uncomfortable\".\nThe remarks by State Minister for Foreign Affairs Humaiun Kobir came two days after Bangladesh on Thursday said Prime Minister Tarique Rahman would not participate in the BRICS Summit hosted by India as he was not invited to the event, with the invitation instead extended to the BIMSTEC chair.\nThe two-day BRICS Summit concluded on Sunday. India had invited Rahman to attend the summit as chairman of the Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation (BIMSTEC), while a separate bilateral invitation had been in place since February.\nBangladesh wants to \"reset\" its bilateral relationship with India, Kobir told reporters here.\n\"We want to move towards a new relationship, which should be done through bilateral discussions,",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-13T17:50:29"
    }
  ]
